message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Change-point transmission and parameter identifiability in an SEIR model of the 2023–2024 West Midlands measles outbreak"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Adeyemi
    given-names: Paul
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24560052"
repository-code: "https://github.com/laplacepaul/west-midlands-measles-seir"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - mathematical epidemiology
  - SEIR model
  - measles
  - parameter identifiability
  - profile likelihood
  - change-point model
  - mathematical biology
abstract: >-
  Retrospective SEIR modelling of the 2023–2024 West Midlands measles outbreak
  using UKHSA onset-week surveillance data. Compares constant and one-change
  transmission specifications, separates structural from practical
  identifiability with independently verified profile likelihoods, and shows
  that the two specifications reproduce the epidemic turnover by different
  mechanisms (susceptible depletion versus a fall in transmission).
